//  withlib.ax -- a program that pulls in shared libraries, so the packer's library loop runs.
//
//  `hello.ax` and `args.ax` have no dependencies at all: `acvm deps` prints nothing for them,
//  which meant every test passed while the code that finds, copies and verifies a shared
//  object was never executed. That code spelled the file name itself -- ".dll" in eight
//  places -- and would have failed on Linux at the copy, after compiling and verifying
//  successfully.
//
//  Importing `os` is enough: it depends on `io`, and both are real shared objects. The output
//  is the platform's name, so the assertion is about behaviour rather than about a constant.

function import (return:(os));

function main():void {
    print(platformName());
    print("\n");
    eof: pass;
}
